  {
   "unit_id": "eng.t_base.phonics.blends-digraphs",
   "title_zh": "子音連綴與二合字母（blends：bl／st／tr…；digraphs：sh／ch／th／ck／ng）",
   "can_do": "我能分辨 blend（子音連綴，像 bl、st、tr——兩個子音各自的音都還聽得到）和 digraph（子音二合字母，像 sh、ch、th、ck、ng——兩個字母合成一個新的音），並讀出這些字。",
   "situation_group": "自然發音：子音連綴與二合字母",
   "subject": "eng",
   "strand": "phonics",
   "est_minutes": 12,
   "knowledge_point_ids": [
    "eng.t_base.phonics.consonant-blends",
    "eng.t_base.phonics.consonant-digraphs"
   ],
   "prerequisites": ["eng.t_base.phonics.cvc-blending"],
   "reuse_pages": [],

   "claims": [
    {"claim_id": "c-blend-twosounds", "text": "A consonant blend is two (or three) consonant letters together where each consonant keeps its own sound, so you can still hear both: 'bl' in blue is /b/ + /l/, 'st' in stop is /s/ + /t/, 'fr' in frog is /f/ + /r/, 'tr' in tree is /t/ + /r/.",
     "kind": "language-usage", "source_refs": ["Cambridge Dictionary"],
     "verification_ref": "子音連綴（blend）＝兩個（或三個）子音字母排在一起、每個子音各自發音仍聽得到：bl（blue）＝/b/＋/l/、st（stop）＝/s/＋/t/、fr（frog）＝/f/＋/r/、tr（tree）＝/t/＋/r/；採美式／KK；Cambridge Dictionary 讀音可查；待英語母語 reviewer 複核", "risk_class": "normal", "status": "provisional"},
    {"claim_id": "c-digraph-onesound", "text": "A consonant digraph is two letters that together make one new sound, not two: 'sh' spells /ʃ/ (ship), and 'ch' spells /tʃ/ (chip, chin, much).",
     "kind": "language-usage", "source_refs": ["Cambridge Dictionary"],
     "verification_ref": "子音二合字母（digraph）＝兩個字母合成一個新音（非兩個）：sh 發 /ʃ/（ship）、ch 發 /tʃ/（chip／chin／much）；誠實標 ch 例外——school 的 ch 發 /k/、chef 的 ch 發 /ʃ/，故 teach 只用乾淨例 chip／chin／much；Cambridge Dictionary 讀音可查；待英語母語 reviewer 複核", "risk_class": "normal", "status": "provisional"},
    {"claim_id": "c-digraph-th-two", "text": "The digraph 'th' spells two different sounds: a voiceless /θ/ as in thin and bath, and a voiced /ð/ as in this, that, and mother.",
     "kind": "language-usage", "source_refs": ["Cambridge Dictionary"],
     "verification_ref": "二合字母 th 有兩個讀音：清音（voiceless）/θ/ 如 thin／bath，濁音（voiced）/ð/ 如 this／that／mother；誠實標出清濁兩讀、不教成單一音；Cambridge Dictionary 讀音可查；待英語母語 reviewer 複核", "risk_class": "normal", "status": "provisional"},
    {"claim_id": "c-digraph-ck-ng", "text": "The digraph 'ck' spells /k/ (duck, sock) and usually comes after a short vowel; the digraph 'ng' spells the single nasal sound /ŋ/ (sing, ring, king).",
     "kind": "language-usage", "source_refs": ["Cambridge Dictionary"],
     "verification_ref": "二合字母 ck 發 /k/（duck／sock），通常接在短母音後；ng 發單一鼻音 /ŋ/（sing／ring／king）；Cambridge Dictionary 讀音可查；待英語母語 reviewer 複核", "risk_class": "normal", "status": "provisional"},
    {"claim_id": "c-blend-vs-digraph", "text": "The key difference: in a blend you hear each consonant's own sound (st = /s/ + /t/), but in a digraph the two letters join into one new sound (sh = /ʃ/).",
     "kind": "language-usage", "source_refs": ["Cambridge Dictionary"],
     "verification_ref": "連綴與二合字母的關鍵差別：blend 聽得到每個子音各自的音（st＝/s/＋/t/），digraph 兩個字母合成一個新音（sh＝/ʃ/）；phonics 通行區辨；Cambridge Dictionary 讀音可查；待英語母語 reviewer 複核", "risk_class": "normal", "status": "provisional"}
   ],

   "teach": [
    {"kind": "text", "kp_ids": ["eng.t_base.phonics.consonant-blends"],
     "body": "A consonant blend is two consonant letters that come together, and you can still hear each one's sound. For example, 'bl' blends /b/ and /l/ in blue, 'st' blends /s/ and /t/ in stop, 'fr' blends /f/ and /r/ in frog, and 'tr' blends /t/ and /r/ in tree. Say the two sounds quickly, one right after the other.",
     "zh_hint": "子音連綴（blend）是兩個子音字母排在一起，而且你還聽得到每一個子音的音。例如：bl 把 /b/ 和 /l/ 連起來（blue）、st 把 /s/ 和 /t/ 連起來（stop）、fr 把 /f/ 和 /r/ 連起來（frog）、tr 把 /t/ 和 /r/ 連起來（tree）。兩個音要快快地、一個接著一個唸。"},
    {"kind": "example", "kp_ids": ["eng.t_base.phonics.consonant-blends"], "audio": "ph_bld_ex1",
     "body": "blue, stop, frog, tree.",
     "zh_hint": "聽每個字開頭的連綴，兩個子音都聽得到：blue（bl）、stop（st）、frog（fr）、tree（tr）。"},
    {"kind": "text", "kp_ids": ["eng.t_base.phonics.consonant-digraphs"],
     "body": "A consonant digraph is different: two letters join to make one new sound, not two. 'sh' makes /ʃ/ in ship, and 'ch' makes /tʃ/ in chip, chin, and much. So in a blend you hear both letters, but in a digraph you hear just one new sound.",
     "zh_hint": "子音二合字母（digraph）不一樣：兩個字母合起來只發一個新的音，不是兩個。sh 發 /ʃ/（ship）、ch 發 /tʃ/（chip、chin、much）。所以連綴聽得到兩個字母的音，二合字母只聽到一個新音。"},
    {"kind": "example", "kp_ids": ["eng.t_base.phonics.consonant-digraphs"], "audio": "ph_bld_ex2",
     "body": "ship, chip, much.",
     "zh_hint": "聽二合字母合成的一個新音：ship（sh＝/ʃ/）、chip、much（ch＝/tʃ/）。"},
    {"kind": "text", "kp_ids": ["eng.t_base.phonics.consonant-digraphs"],
     "body": "The digraph 'th' has two sounds: a quiet, breathy /θ/ in thin, and a buzzing /ð/ in this. Two more digraphs: 'ck' makes /k/ in duck, and 'ng' makes one nasal sound /ŋ/ in sing.",
     "zh_hint": "二合字母 th 有兩個音：輕輕吹氣的清音 /θ/（thin），和會震動的濁音 /ð/（this）。另外兩個二合字母：ck 發 /k/（duck）、ng 發一個鼻音 /ŋ/（sing）。"},
    {"kind": "example", "kp_ids": ["eng.t_base.phonics.consonant-digraphs"], "audio": "ph_bld_ex3",
     "body": "thin, this, duck, sing.",
     "zh_hint": "聽：thin 的 th 是清音 /θ/、this 的 th 是濁音 /ð/；duck 的 ck 是 /k/；sing 的 ng 是 /ŋ/。"}
   ],

