  {
   "unit_id": "eng.t_base.phonics.schwa-and-stress",
   "title_zh": "弱化音 schwa 與單字重音",
   "can_do": "我能聽出多音節字裡哪個音節比較重，也能聽出沒重讀的音節常常變成模糊、輕輕的 schwa /ə/ 音（像 about、sofa、banana 裡的 a）。",
   "situation_group": "自然發音：弱音與重音",
   "subject": "eng",
   "strand": "phonics",
   "est_minutes": 10,
   "knowledge_point_ids": [
    "eng.t_base.phonics.schwa",
    "eng.t_base.phonics.syllable-stress"
   ],
   "prerequisites": ["eng.t_base.phonics.cvc-blending"],
   "reuse_pages": [],

   "claims": [
    {"claim_id": "c-schwa-def", "text": "The schwa /ə/ is the short, weak vowel in a syllable that is not stressed. It sounds like a soft 'uh'. You hear it in the first 'a' of about /əˈbaʊt/ and the last 'a' of sofa /ˈsoʊfə/.",
     "kind": "language-usage", "source_refs": ["Cambridge Dictionary"],
     "verification_ref": "schwa /ə/ 是非重讀音節裡短而弱的模糊母音（像輕輕的「ə」）；about /əˈbaʊt/ 的首 a、sofa /ˈsoʊfə/ 的尾 a 皆為 schwa；採美式／KK；Cambridge Dictionary 讀音可查；待英語母語 reviewer 複核", "risk_class": "normal", "status": "provisional"},
    {"claim_id": "c-schwa-any-vowel", "text": "Any vowel letter (a, e, i, o, u) can be read as the schwa /ə/ when its syllable is weak and unstressed. Schwa is not tied to one special letter; it depends on stress, not spelling. In banana /bəˈnænə/ the first and last 'a' are both schwa.",
     "kind": "language-usage", "source_refs": ["Cambridge Dictionary"],
     "verification_ref": "任何母音字母（a／e／i／o／u）在弱讀、非重讀音節都可能讀成 schwa /ə/；schwa 由「重音」決定、不綁特定字母（不是某字母專屬）；banana /bəˈnænə/ 首尾 a 皆 schwa；誠實標出『由弱讀產生、非拼字決定』；Cambridge Dictionary 讀音可查；待英語母語 reviewer 複核", "risk_class": "normal", "status": "provisional"},
    {"claim_id": "c-syllable-stress", "text": "A word with more than one syllable has a stressed syllable (said a little louder, longer and clearer) and one or more unstressed syllables. For example 'table' is TA-ble (stress first) and 'banana' is ba-NA-na (stress middle). The unstressed syllables often shrink to the weak schwa /ə/.",
     "kind": "language-usage", "source_refs": ["Cambridge Dictionary"],
     "verification_ref": "多音節字有重讀音節（唸得較大聲、較長、較清楚）與一或多個非重讀音節；table＝TA-ble（重音在首）、banana＝ba-NA-na（重音在中）；非重讀音節常弱化成 schwa /ə/；採美式／KK；Cambridge Dictionary 重音標記與讀音可查；待英語母語 reviewer 複核", "risk_class": "normal", "status": "provisional"},
    {"claim_id": "c-stress-noun-verb", "text": "For a small number of words that are spelled the same, moving the stress changes whether the word is a noun or a verb, for example REcord (noun) and reCORD (verb). This is only true for a few words, so at this level just focus on hearing which syllable sounds stronger.",
     "kind": "language-usage", "source_refs": ["Cambridge Dictionary"],
     "verification_ref": "少數同拼寫字移動重音會改變名詞/動詞，如 REcord（名詞 /ˈrɛkɚd/）vs reCORD（動詞 /rɪˈkɔrd/）；此名動對比僅適用少數字、保守處理，初級聚焦『聽出哪個音節較重』；採美式／KK；Cambridge Dictionary 讀音可查；待英語母語 reviewer 複核", "risk_class": "normal", "status": "provisional"}
   ],

   "teach": [
    {"kind": "text", "kp_ids": ["eng.t_base.phonics.schwa"],
     "body": "English has a very common weak vowel called the schwa, written /ə/. It is a short, soft 'uh' sound that you make in a syllable you do not stress. Listen for it in the first 'a' of about /əˈbaʊt/ and the last 'a' of sofa /ˈsoʊfə/.",
     "zh_hint": "英文有一個很常見的「弱母音」叫做 schwa，寫成 /ə/。它是一個短短、輕輕、像「ə」的音，出現在你沒有重讀的音節裡。聽聽看 about /əˈbaʊt/ 的第一個 a，還有 sofa /ˈsoʊfə/ 的最後一個 a。"},
    {"kind": "text", "kp_ids": ["eng.t_base.phonics.schwa"],
     "body": "The schwa is not tied to one letter. Any vowel letter can become /ə/ when its syllable is weak, so it depends on the stress, not the spelling. In banana /bəˈnænə/, the first and last 'a' are both the weak schwa, while only the middle part is strong.",
     "zh_hint": "schwa 不綁定某一個字母。任何母音字母在弱讀的音節裡都可能變成 /ə/，所以它看的是「重音」而不是「拼法」。在 banana /bəˈnænə/ 裡，第一個和最後一個 a 都是弱弱的 schwa，只有中間那段比較重。"},
    {"kind": "example", "kp_ids": ["eng.t_base.phonics.schwa"], "audio": "ph_sch_ex1",
     "body": "about, sofa, banana.",
     "zh_hint": "聽弱弱的 schwa /ə/：about（首 a）、sofa（尾 a）、banana（首尾 a 都是）。"},
    {"kind": "text", "kp_ids": ["eng.t_base.phonics.syllable-stress"],
     "body": "A word with more than one syllable has one strong (stressed) syllable and one or more weak (unstressed) ones. The strong syllable is a little louder, longer and clearer. We say 'table' as TA-ble (strong first) and 'banana' as ba-NA-na (strong middle). The weak syllables often become the schwa /ə/, which is how the two ideas connect.",
     "zh_hint": "超過一個音節的字，會有一個「比較重」的音節和一或多個「比較輕」的音節。重的音節唸得稍微大聲、長一點、清楚一點。table 唸成 TA-ble（第一個重）、banana 唸成 ba-NA-na（中間重）。輕的音節常常就變成 schwa /ə/——這就是弱音和重音連在一起的地方。"},
    {"kind": "example", "kp_ids": ["eng.t_base.phonics.syllable-stress"], "audio": "ph_sch_ex2",
     "body": "table, banana, computer.",
     "zh_hint": "聽哪個音節比較重：table（TA-ble，前重）、banana（ba-NA-na，中重）、computer（com-PU-ter，中重）。"}
   ],

   "practice": [
    {"question_id": "P1-schwa-about", "type": "mcq", "validation_method": "expert",
     "stem": "about 的第一個 a（沒有重讀）發哪個弱弱的母音？", "answer": "/ə/（schwa，輕輕的「ə」）",
     "kp_ids": ["eng.t_base.phonics.schwa"], "required_kp_ids": ["eng.t_base.phonics.schwa"],
     "options": ["/ə/（schwa，輕輕的「ə」）", "/æ/（像 cat 的 a）", "/eɪ/（像字母 A 的名字）", "/ɑ/（像 father 的 a）"],
     "distractor_rationales": {
      "/æ/（像 cat 的 a）": "/æ/ 是重讀短母音（cat），about 的首 a 沒重讀、會弱化成 schwa。",
      "/eɪ/（像字母 A 的名字）": "/eɪ/ 是字母 A 的「名字」音，不是這裡弱讀的音。",
      "/ɑ/（像 father 的 a）": "/ɑ/ 是重讀的開口母音，about 的首 a 是弱讀的 schwa /ə/。"},
     "answer_evidence": ["c-schwa-def"],
     "feedback": "about /əˈbaʊt/ 的首 a 沒重讀，弱化成 schwa /ə/。"},

    {"question_id": "P2-schwa-any-vowel", "type": "mcq", "validation_method": "expert",
     "stem": "關於 schwa /ə/，下面哪一句是對的？", "answer": "任何母音字母在弱讀（沒重音）的音節裡都可能發成 /ə/。",
     "kp_ids": ["eng.t_base.phonics.schwa"], "required_kp_ids": ["eng.t_base.phonics.schwa"],
     "options": ["任何母音字母在弱讀（沒重音）的音節裡都可能發成 /ə/。", "只有字母 a 才會發 schwa /ə/。", "schwa 只出現在重讀的音節裡。", "schwa 是一個子音。"],
     "distractor_rationales": {
      "只有字母 a 才會發 schwa /ə/。": "不只 a——a／e／i／o／u 任何母音字母在弱讀時都可能是 schwa。",
      "schwa 只出現在重讀的音節裡。": "剛好相反：schwa 出現在「沒有重讀」的弱音節裡。",
      "schwa 是一個子音。": "schwa /ə/ 是母音（弱弱的母音），不是子音。"},
     "answer_evidence": ["c-schwa-any-vowel"],
     "feedback": "schwa 由「弱讀」產生、不綁特定字母：a／e／i／o／u 在沒重音的音節都可能讀 /ə/。"},

    {"question_id": "P3-stress-banana", "type": "mcq", "validation_method": "expert",
     "stem": "banana 這個字，哪一個音節唸起來最重？", "answer": "中間的 na（ba-NA-na）",
     "kp_ids": ["eng.t_base.phonics.syllable-stress"], "required_kp_ids": ["eng.t_base.phonics.syllable-stress"],
     "options": ["中間的 na（ba-NA-na）", "第一個 ba", "最後的 na", "三個一樣重"],
     "distractor_rationales": {
      "第一個 ba": "第一個 ba 是弱讀的 schwa /bə/，不是最重的。",
      "最後的 na": "最後的 na 也弱讀成 /nə/，不是最重的。",
      "三個一樣重": "多音節字通常只有一個音節最重，banana 的重音在中間。"},
     "answer_evidence": ["c-syllable-stress"],
     "feedback": "banana＝ba-NA-na，重音在中間的 na；前後兩個 a 都弱化成 schwa /ə/。"},

    {"question_id": "P4-stress-dictation", "type": "dictation", "validation_method": "expert",
     "stem": "聽音檔，把你聽到的字寫下來，並圈出聽起來最重的音節。", "answer": "banana（重音在中間：ba-NA-na）",
     "audio": "ph_sch_dict01",
     "kp_ids": ["eng.t_base.phonics.syllable-stress"], "required_kp_ids": ["eng.t_base.phonics.syllable-stress"],
     "feedback": "對照答案自評：聽到 /bəˈnænə/，字是 banana，最重的音節是中間的 NA（ba-NA-na）。寫對、也聽對重音了嗎？"}
   ],

   "selfeval": ["還不熟", "快會了", "會了"],
