  {
   "unit_id": "eng.t_base.phonics.ed-and-plural-s",
   "title_zh": "過去式 -ed 與複數/三單 -s 的三種發音",
   "can_do": "我能聽出並判斷規則過去式 -ed 的三種音（/t/、/d/、/ɪd/），以及複數／三單 -s/-es 的三種音（/s/、/z/、/ɪz/），知道是看「前一個音」來決定。",
   "situation_group": "自然發音：字尾 -ed 與 -s",
   "subject": "eng",
   "strand": "phonics",
   "est_minutes": 11,
   "knowledge_point_ids": [
    "eng.t_base.phonics.ed-sound",
    "eng.t_base.phonics.plural-s-sound"
   ],
   "prerequisites": ["eng.t_base.phonics.cvc-blending"],
   "reuse_pages": [],

   "claims": [
    {"claim_id": "c-ed-three", "text": "The regular past-tense ending -ed is spelled the same but said in three ways: /t/ in walked, /d/ in played, and an extra syllable /ɪd/ in wanted and needed.",
     "kind": "language-usage", "source_refs": ["Cambridge Dictionary"],
     "verification_ref": "規則過去式字尾 -ed 拼法相同但有三種唸法：walked /t/、played /d/、wanted/needed 多一個音節 /ɪd/；採美式／KK；Cambridge Dictionary 讀音可查；待英語母語 reviewer 複核", "risk_class": "normal", "status": "provisional"},
    {"claim_id": "c-ed-criterion", "text": "Which -ed sound you use depends on the last SOUND of the base verb, not the spelling: after a voiceless sound it is /t/ (walked), after a voiced sound or a vowel it is /d/ (played), and after the sounds /t/ or /d/ it adds a whole syllable /ɪd/ (wanted, needed). Some dictionaries write this ending as /əd/ with a schwa.",
     "kind": "language-usage", "source_refs": ["Cambridge Dictionary"],
     "verification_ref": "-ed 唸哪個音看原形動詞『最後一個音』的清濁（不是看拼字）：清音後 /t/（walked）、濁音或母音後 /d/（played）、/t/ 或 /d/ 音後加一整個音節 /ɪd/（wanted／needed）；誠實標出判準＝前一個音的清濁；部分字典把此結尾寫成 schwa /əd/；採美式／KK；Cambridge Dictionary 讀音可查；待英語母語 reviewer 複核", "risk_class": "normal", "status": "provisional"},
    {"claim_id": "c-plural-three", "text": "The plural or third-person -s/-es ending is also said in three ways: /s/ in cats, /z/ in dogs, and an extra syllable /ɪz/ in buses and boxes.",
     "kind": "language-usage", "source_refs": ["Cambridge Dictionary"],
     "verification_ref": "複數／三單字尾 -s/-es 也有三種唸法：cats /s/、dogs /z/、buses/boxes 多一個音節 /ɪz/；採美式／KK；Cambridge Dictionary 讀音可查；待英語母語 reviewer 複核", "risk_class": "normal", "status": "provisional"},
    {"claim_id": "c-plural-criterion", "text": "Which -s sound you use also depends on the last SOUND of the word: after a voiceless sound it is /s/ (cats), after a voiced sound or a vowel it is /z/ (dogs), and after a hissing (sibilant) sound such as s, z, sh, ch, or x it adds a syllable /ɪz/ (buses, boxes). Some dictionaries write this ending as /əz/ with a schwa.",
     "kind": "language-usage", "source_refs": ["Cambridge Dictionary"],
     "verification_ref": "-s 唸哪個音也看字『最後一個音』：清音後 /s/（cats）、濁音或母音後 /z/（dogs）、嘶擦音 s／z／sh／ch／x 後加一音節 /ɪz/（buses／boxes）；誠實標出判準＝前一個音（清濁／是否嘶擦音）；部分字典寫成 schwa /əz/；採美式／KK；Cambridge Dictionary 讀音可查；待英語母語 reviewer 複核", "risk_class": "normal", "status": "provisional"}
   ],

   "teach": [
    {"kind": "text", "kp_ids": ["eng.t_base.phonics.ed-sound"],
     "body": "Regular past-tense verbs end in -ed, but the ending is said in three ways. The trick is to listen to the last SOUND of the base verb, not the spelling. After a quiet (voiceless) sound it is /t/, as in walked. After a buzzing (voiced) sound or a vowel it is /d/, as in played. After a /t/ or /d/ sound it adds a whole extra syllable /ɪd/, as in wanted and needed.",
     "zh_hint": "規則過去式動詞字尾是 -ed，但有三種唸法。訣竅是聽原形動詞『最後一個音』，不是看拼字。清清的（無聲帶振動的）音後面唸 /t/，像 walked；濁濁的（有聲帶振動的）音或母音後面唸 /d/，像 played；在 /t/ 或 /d/ 音後面，會多加一整個音節 /ɪd/，像 wanted、needed。（有些字典把這個 /ɪd/ 寫成 schwa /əd/。）"},
    {"kind": "example", "kp_ids": ["eng.t_base.phonics.ed-sound"], "audio": "ph_ed_ex1",
     "body": "walked, played, wanted.",
     "zh_hint": "聽 -ed 的三種音：walked（/t/）、played（/d/）、wanted（多一音節 /ɪd/）。"},
    {"kind": "text", "kp_ids": ["eng.t_base.phonics.plural-s-sound"],
     "body": "The plural and the third-person -s/-es ending works the same way, with three sounds decided by the last sound of the word. After a quiet (voiceless) sound it is /s/, as in cats. After a buzzing (voiced) sound or a vowel it is /z/, as in dogs. After a hissing sound such as s, z, sh, ch, or x it adds a syllable /ɪz/, as in buses and boxes.",
     "zh_hint": "複數和三單的 -s/-es 字尾也一樣，有三種音，由字的『最後一個音』決定。清清的（無聲）音後面唸 /s/，像 cats；濁濁的（有聲）音或母音後面唸 /z/，像 dogs；在嘶嘶的音（s、z、sh、ch、x）後面會多加一音節 /ɪz/，像 buses、boxes。（有些字典寫成 schwa /əz/。）"},
    {"kind": "example", "kp_ids": ["eng.t_base.phonics.plural-s-sound"], "audio": "ph_ed_ex2",
     "body": "cats, dogs, buses.",
     "zh_hint": "聽 -s 的三種音：cats（/s/）、dogs（/z/）、buses（多一音節 /ɪz/）。"}
   ],

   "practice": [
