  {
   "unit_id": "eng.t_mid.phonics.kk-ipa",
   "title_zh": "看懂字典音標：KK 與 IPA",
   "can_do": "我能看懂字典裡的發音符號——知道台灣常用的 KK 音標和國際 IPA 是兩套不同系統，會對照母音與子音符號、看懂重音記號 ˈ，用音標把字典裡的字唸出來。",
   "situation_group": "自然發音：看懂字典音標",
   "subject": "eng",
   "strand": "phonics",
   "est_minutes": 10,
   "knowledge_point_ids": [
    "eng.t_mid.phonics.kk-ipa"
   ],
   "prerequisites": ["eng.t_base.phonics.cvc-blending"],
   "reuse_pages": [],

   "claims": [
    {"claim_id": "c-what-are-symbols", "text": "A dictionary shows how to say a word using special pronunciation symbols inside slashes, for example cat /kæt/. Each symbol stands for one sound, so once you know the symbols you can say a new word correctly from the dictionary.",
     "kind": "language-usage", "source_refs": ["Cambridge Dictionary", "Oxford Learner's Dictionaries"],
     "verification_ref": "字典用斜線內的發音符號標出怎麼唸，如 cat /kæt/；每個符號代表一個音，看懂符號就能照字典把新字唸對；基礎事實；待英語母語 reviewer 複核", "risk_class": "normal", "status": "provisional"},
    {"claim_id": "c-kk-vs-ipa", "text": "There are two common systems. KK (from Kenyon & Knott) describes American English pronunciation and is the system many Taiwan dictionaries use. IPA, the International Phonetic Alphabet, is used around the world, for example by the Cambridge and Oxford dictionaries. They are two different systems, not the same one.",
     "kind": "language-usage", "source_refs": ["Kenyon & Knott, A Pronouncing Dictionary of American English", "Cambridge Dictionary"],
     "verification_ref": "常見有兩套系統：KK（Kenyon & Knott）描述美式發音、台灣許多字典採用；IPA 國際音標全世界通用、如 Cambridge／Oxford 字典採用；兩者是不同系統（非同一套）；誠實標出『不同字典用不同系統』；待英語母語 reviewer 複核", "risk_class": "normal", "status": "provisional"},
    {"claim_id": "c-stress-mark", "text": "In both systems a small vertical mark ˈ is placed just before a syllable to show that this syllable is stressed (said a little stronger), for example banana /bəˈnænə/, where the mark is before the middle syllable.",
     "kind": "language-usage", "source_refs": ["Cambridge Dictionary", "Oxford Learner's Dictionaries"],
     "verification_ref": "兩套系統都用一個小直線記號 ˈ 放在某音節『前面』表示該音節重讀（唸得較重），如 banana /bəˈnænə/，記號在中間音節前；重音記號慣例可查字典；待英語母語 reviewer 複核", "risk_class": "normal", "status": "provisional"},
    {"claim_id": "c-kk-ipa-differences", "text": "Many symbols look the same in both systems (for example /p/, /b/, /m/, and the short vowels /ɪ/, /ɛ/, /ʊ/). But some vowels are written differently. Two examples: (1) for the long vowel in see, IPA adds a length mark ː and writes /siː/, while KK writes /si/ with no ː; (2) for the vowels in name and go, IPA uses gliding pairs /eɪ/ and /oʊ/, while KK uses single letters /e/ and /o/ (so KK writes name /nem/ and go /ɡo/). The sound is the same; only the symbol differs. Because of this, always check the key in the dictionary you are using.",
     "kind": "language-usage", "source_refs": ["Kenyon & Knott, A Pronouncing Dictionary of American English", "Cambridge Dictionary"],
     "verification_ref": "許多符號兩套一樣（如 /p/／/b/／/m/ 與短母音 /ɪ/／/ɛ/／/ʊ/）；但有些母音寫法不同，兩個例子：(1) see 的長母音 IPA 加長音記號 ː 寫 /siː/、KK 寫 /si/ 不加 ː；(2) name、go 的母音 IPA 用滑音 /eɪ/、/oʊ/，KK 用單母音符號 /e/、/o/（KK：name /nem/、go /ɡo/）——同一個音、只是符號不同（name/go 本就無 ː，差別在滑音 vs 單母音符號，非長音記號）；誠實標出『不同字典用不同系統，要看該字典的音標對照表』；待英語母語 reviewer 複核", "risk_class": "normal", "status": "provisional"}
   ],

   "teach": [
    {"kind": "text", "kp_ids": ["eng.t_mid.phonics.kk-ipa"],
     "body": "When you look up a word, the dictionary shows how to say it with special symbols inside slashes, like cat /kæt/. Each symbol stands for one sound. Once you can read the symbols, you can say a brand-new word correctly straight from the dictionary.",
     "zh_hint": "查單字時，字典會用斜線裡的特殊符號告訴你怎麼唸，像 cat /kæt/。每個符號代表一個音。只要會看這些符號，就算是沒看過的新字，也能照著字典唸對。"},
    {"kind": "text", "kp_ids": ["eng.t_mid.phonics.kk-ipa"],
     "body": "There are two common systems. KK (from Kenyon & Knott) is for American English and is used in many Taiwan dictionaries. IPA, the International Phonetic Alphabet, is used around the world, for example by Cambridge and Oxford. They are two different systems, so first check which one your dictionary uses. Good news: many symbols are the same, like the consonants /p/, /b/, /m/ and the short vowels /ɪ/, /ɛ/, /ʊ/.",
     "zh_hint": "常見有兩套系統。KK（來自 Kenyon & Knott）是給美式英語用的，台灣很多字典採用；IPA（國際音標）全世界通用，像 Cambridge、Oxford 字典。這是兩套不同的系統，所以要先看你的字典用哪一套。好消息是：很多符號兩套都一樣，像子音 /p/、/b/、/m/ 和短母音 /ɪ/、/ɛ/、/ʊ/。"},
    {"kind": "text", "kp_ids": ["eng.t_mid.phonics.kk-ipa"],
     "body": "A small upright mark ˈ goes just before a syllable to show it is the stressed one, said a little stronger. In banana /bəˈnænə/ the mark is before the middle syllable, so we say ba-NA-na. Finding this mark tells you where to push a word.",
     "zh_hint": "一個小小的直線記號 ˈ 會放在某個音節『前面』，表示那個音節要重讀、唸得重一點。在 banana /bəˈnænə/ 裡，記號在中間音節前，所以唸 ba-NA-na。找到這個記號，就知道一個字要把力氣放在哪裡。"},
    {"kind": "text", "kp_ids": ["eng.t_mid.phonics.kk-ipa"],
     "body": "Some vowels are written differently in the two systems. For the long vowel in see, IPA adds a length mark ː and writes /siː/, while KK writes /si/ with no ː. For the vowels in name and go, IPA uses gliding pairs, /neɪm/ and /ɡoʊ/, while KK uses single letters, /nem/ and /ɡo/. The sound is the same; only the symbol looks different — so always read the pronunciation key printed in your own dictionary.",
     "zh_hint": "有些母音兩套寫法不同。see 的長母音，IPA 加長音記號 ː 寫成 /siː/，KK 寫成 /si/ 不加 ː。name、go 的母音，IPA 用滑音寫成 /neɪm/、/ɡoʊ/，KK 用單母音符號寫成 /nem/、/ɡo/。同一個音、符號看起來不同——所以記得看你那本字典裡印的『音標對照表』。"},
    {"kind": "example", "kp_ids": ["eng.t_mid.phonics.kk-ipa"], "audio": "ph_kk_ex1",
     "body": "cat, see, book.",
     "zh_hint": "照音標唸出來：cat /kæt/、see /siː/、book /bʊk/（對照字典符號和你聽到的音）。"}
   ],

